      "content": "While specific cultural factors vary widely, high-density, lower-income communities often experience heightened necessity for close socialization and communal activities. In environments with fewer resources, people may rely more heavily on shared informal networks rather than private medical settings. Additionally, reliance on public transit in District 3 or crowded living situations in District 4 naturally forces more frequent, close-contact interactions compared to the sprawling, low-density settings of North Hills.",
      "source": "target",
